1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,426
The Output tab holds every file the job makes, plus the export check.

2
00:00:07,426 --> 00:00:11,110
First, a reminder: these programs are not machine-proven. Simulate every one in woodWOP.

3
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:15,229
MPR programs stay greyed out until you tick the simulate box, and while the check finds any errors.

4
00:00:15,229 --> 00:00:17,081
Validation lists every problem: red errors block export, amber warnings need a look.

5
00:00:17,081 --> 00:00:21,333
This job has 0 errors. An error would be, say, two parts closer than the cut-out tool needs.

6
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:25,667
Warnings: placeholder tools, small parts that vacuum may not hold, holes to drill by hand.

7
00:00:25,667 --> 00:00:31,166
Configure badges mark placeholder values still to be set up. Click one...

8
00:00:31,166 --> 00:00:35,522
...and it jumps straight to that value on the Machine page, ready to fill in.

9
00:00:35,522 --> 00:00:45,084
Back on the job, the Programs list has one woodWOP MPR file per sheet.

10
00:00:45,084 --> 00:00:53,961
Open shows the program as generated, the same text woodWOP will read.

11
00:00:53,961 --> 00:01:02,104
Check reads the program back: toolpaths, moves, and whether it stays on the table.

12
00:01:02,104 --> 00:01:07,858
Nothing goes to the N-200 until the real tool table is in and you tick this box.
